==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈvaɪ̯tsən/|[ˈväɪ̯.t͡sən]|[ˈʋäɪ̯-]|[-t͡sn̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Weizen.ogg|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|weize}}, {{m|gmh|weizze}}, {{m|gmh|weitze}}, from {{inh|de|goh|weizi}}, {{m|goh|weizzi}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*hwaitijaz}}, which is related with {{m|gem-pro|*hwītaz||white}}. The originally predominant High German form was {{m|de|Weiße|Weiße(n)}} (perhaps still in {{m|de|Weißbier}}; see there). The form with {{IPAchar|[ts]}} was a chiefly southern variant, which was standardised probably to avoid the homophony with the adjective {{m|de|weiß}}. Cognate with {{cog|lb|Weess}}, {{cog|nl|weit}}, {{cog|nds|Weten}}, {{cog|fy|weet}}, {{cog|en|wheat}}.

